  "rationale": "The hard constraints (throughput_msps >= 32 and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44) are throughput/latency constraints that only the 1-result/cycle families can meet; iterative and unrolled_k emit one result every several cycles and would be screened out, so I exclude them to spend the full 400-eval budget on the two feasible families. I focus the search on the accuracy/area trade-off: data_width 14-20 and n_iter 12-18 bracket the region where max_abs_err crosses the 2^-12 bound (accuracy_bits ~12-14), which is exactly where the min-luts_plus_ffs objective and the max-accuracy_bits objective pull in opposite directions. angle_guard 0-2 and frac_guard 0-2 give the small accuracy/area levers without wasting budget on wide guards that only inflate area. Rounding is left to both options since it is a cheap accuracy/area toggle. The two families are searched with equal weight because pipelined anchors the baseline and pipelined_m adds the FF/Fmax trade-off dimension; together they should map the feasible Pareto front over the spec's objectives. The front will then be screened at L1 and the shortlist simulated at L2 for the 0.44 us batch deadline."
